From e5e9f2be4dbc03c0c4aa82445aced9904dc7ab4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:30:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: Add a stateless H.264 encoder

Add v4l2slh264enc for encoders that implement the H.264 stateless encode
uAPI (V4L2_CID_STATELESS_H264_ENCODE_PARAMS): the RK3588 VEPU580
(rockchip-venc) and the Hantro H1.

With that uAPI the kernel writes the parameter sets and slice headers,
keeps the reconstructed reference picture and runs the rate control, so
the element only sets the SPS and PPS once and describes each picture
(slice type, IDR, frame_num, picture order count) in its request.

The common part of the encoders is the abstract GstV4l2CodecBaseEnc
class, a GstVideoEncoder that negotiates the formats, imports or copies
the input pictures, keeps up to max-inflight requests queued (2 by
default, so the driver always has the next picture while userspace
completes the previous one), finishes the pictures in order and offers
its buffer pool upstream for zero-copy input. It provides the rate
control modes:

- cqp: constant QP (qp-i, qp-p), the driver rate control disabled;
- cbr: the driver's constant bitrate rate control, within qp-min and
  qp-max;
- vbr: a frame-level rate control in the element that sets the QP of
  each picture in its request: a bits = complexity * 2^(-QP/6) model per
  picture type, corrected by the accumulated error to the target bitrate
  and limited by max-bitrate over one second.

The H.264 encoder produces Constrained Baseline, Main or High profile
(chosen by the downstream caps, High by default) I and P pictures with
one reference picture, CABAC by default on Main and High, an IDR picture
every key-int-max pictures or on request, at the lowest level that fits
the size, frame rate and bitrate.

The profile and level handling derive from the work on stateless
encoders by Michael Grzeschik, Denis Shimizu and Paul Kocialkowski
(gstreamer MR !5676 and the v4l2codecs/h264enc branch of Paul
Kocialkowski), which uses the same uAPI; the element itself is new.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
